// v21.2.43: persistent Pragmatic MULTIPLAY session-conflict recovery. Try the normal "Hier Fortfahren" session control first; if duplicate-connection state persists, reload Betify to force a real server-auth check and then reuse the existing safe login/Baccarat/MULTIPLAY recovery.
// v21.2.44: any new physical Pragmatic MULTIPLAY WebSocket after the 30s baseline/warm-up window with multiTable=true, mtbInGame=true and reconnect=true is treated as an integrity break for currently running side-table shoes. They are immediately marked untrusted and strategy/signals stay disabled until each table reaches a freshly observed endshuffling/new-shoe reset.
// v21.2.45: reconnect-storm guard. Eight or more distinct physical MULTIPLAY reconnect sockets within five seconds (after the startup baseline) are treated as a broken reconnect loop. The app immediately performs the same controlled Betify reload/server-auth validation used by persistent session-conflict recovery instead of waiting 30 seconds while Pragmatic creates hundreds of replacement sockets.
// v21.2.46: login-state priority fix. Visible logged-out controls (password field / Anmelden / Registrierung) now always outrank generic deposit-related page text. Logged-in state requires a visible interactive account action instead of merely finding words such as Einzahlung somewhere in Betify's body text.
// v21.2.95: Betify session-stability fix. Deposit/Withdraw controls are fully neutral during an established session and can never trigger AUTO_LOGOUT_DETECTED or invalidate running shoes. Only visible password/login UI remains authoritative logged-out evidence in the passive Stage-0 watchdog; registration-only/promotional account controls are ambiguous and ignored there.
// v21.2.96: conservative Pragmatic burn tracking. A burn indicator affects Lucky-Pairs composition only after one unambiguous pre-first-betsopen card has been confirmed. Its rank is then removed exactly once; hidden burn ranks remain untouched. The derived physical burn count is tracked separately for cards-out/penetration and never shrinks the predictive rank pool.
// v21.2.97: overview exposes a dedicated Burnkarten column (exact count only after confirmed burn, otherwise "?"). Telegram bot token can be maintained in the UI and is persisted without logging the secret. A one-time session-start Telegram is queued only after Pragmatic MULTIPLAY is both UI-ready and a real multi-table game-progress frame proves that live counting has started.
// v21.2.98: second-source Pragmatic burn probe. During the short post-endshuffling window all text frames for the affected table are captured, including formerly noisy event types such as cardinc/timer/dealer. The primary Baccarat DOM is sampled at high frequency for a single visible rank+suit card; only two consecutive identical single-card samples may become a DOM burn candidate. Ambiguous/no evidence still leaves the proven Edge math untouched.
// v21.2.99: Burn Probe v3 extends the visual evidence channel to the MULTIPLAY table tiles themselves. Active new-shoe tables are located by their exact displayed table name, card-like SVG/image markup is sampled at high frequency, and one structural snapshot is captured per shoe for diagnosis. When available, up to three rendered video JPEGs and three table-matched binary ws1 media frames are retained as diagnostic evidence only. A MULTIPLAY observation can only stage evidence after repeated identical single-card samples followed by disappearance while the same table tile is still present; no safely confirmed card means no Edge change.
